<Base title="Research">
  <h1>Research</h1>
  <p class="lead">Primordial magnetic fields: turbulent decay, reconnection dynamics, and cosmological signatures.</p>

  <h2>Interests</h2>
  <p>
    Primordial magnetic fields and cosmic magnetism: the nonlinear evolution of magnetically dominated MHD
    turbulence, magnetic reconnection, and the effect of primordial fields on cosmological recombination.
  </p>

  <h2>Methods</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Analytical modelling of turbulent decay and reconnection.</li>
    <li>Large-scale simulations with Pencil Code, Dedalus and Athena++.</li>
    <li>Dedalus modules for spectral diagnostics of turbulence, and a modified recombination equation to study the role of primordial fields.</li>
    <li>Python analysis pipelines, including Minkowski functionals on turbulence data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Earlier work</h2>
  <p>
    Holographic entanglement entropy and fluid-gravity duality (M.Sc. thesis at NISER and related papers in JHEP).
  </p>
</Base>
